    "changelog_excerpt": "# 🚀 DMTools Release v1.7.273\n\n## 📝 What's Changed\n\nFull diff: [v1.7.272...v1.7.273](https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/compare/v1.7.272...v1.7.273)\n\n### 🚀 Features\n- Optional Markdown format for descriptions, fields and comments (agents#805) (2fa732d0)\n- Tracker-agnostic ticket operations on Azure DevOps (#661) (e25d9727)\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n- Dmtools --help prints usage instead of opening the interactive picker (#670) (91bd8396)\n\n### 📦 Dependencies\n- Bump smol-toml from 1.7.1 to 1.9.0 in /landing (#666) (07d65ade)\n- Bump source-map-js from 1.2.1 to 1.2.2 in /landing (#665) (92bde747)\n\n### 🛠 Maintenance\n- Bump sharp from 0.35.4 to 0.35.5 in /landing (#667) (b1f148de)\n- Bump submodule to include the ADO-tools fix (dmtools-agents#797) (4e46f888)\n- Bump submodule — every ticket call goes through the tracker layer (#661) (b5f0e869)\n- Run the required 'Java unit tests' check on a GitHub-hosted runner (b44fd02f)\n- Update coverage badge (#669) (90f0592b)\n\n---\n\nThis release includes the **DMTools CLI** and **Agent Skill** for enterprise dark-factory orchestration across MCP tools, AI agents, and delivery workflows.\n\n## 📦 What's Included\n\n### 🖥️ DMTools CLI\n- **Command-line interface** for DMTools operations\n- **Java-based** automation and integration tools\n- **Cross-platform install scripts** for easy setup (`install`, `install.sh`, `install.bat`, `install.ps1`)\n- **Wrapper script** (`dmtools.sh`)\n\n### 🤖 DMTools Agent Skill\n- **AI assistant skill** for MCP, AI agents, and generative-ai-friendly DMTools workflows in Cursor, Claude, Codex, and other Agent Skills compatible systems\n- **Complete DMtools documentation** (67+ MCP tools, JavaScript agent development, and configuration guides)\n- **Cross-platform support** (works with all major AI coding assistants)\n\n## 🎯 Quick Start\n\n### Install DMTools CLI\n\n**macOS / Linux / Git Bash:**\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/latest/download/install.sh | bash\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell):**\n```powershell\nirm https://gi..."
